# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; this template is the only
# env file that should ever be committed — keep real values out of it.
#
# Set either the two Supabase values, or DATABASE_URL alone to use any plain
# Postgres directly (the app then creates its sim_* tables on first use).
# Supabase is used when both are set.

# Server-only. The service-role key bypasses RLS — never prefix either of
# these with NEXT_PUBLIC_, which would ship them to the browser.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Only for `npm run db:setup`, which creates the sim_* tables — the app itself
# never uses it. Supabase dashboard → Connect → Session pooler; put your
# database password in place of [YOUR-PASSWORD]. It holds that password.
# DATABASE_URL=
